# EXPECT: for binder over a NUMERIC module name
# ouroboros#161 (cell 2): a module-scope `for` binder over a numeric module
# name with a STRING iterable. The loop-scoped binder is a C double, so the
# program built and died at run time ("non-numeric value in a numeric
# context at <module>: for-in v (type str)") where the VM prints a b 1.
# Refused by name at build time, as round 120 does inside functions.
v is 1
for v in ["a", "b"]:
    print of v
print of v
